 "table": {
  "mountings": "<p class=\"tcap\">Table 1. The nine mountings on the NREL 5 MW turbine ($\\Gamma = R/G$): the wind and the rotor speed it gives, the pivot as a fraction of the 63 m rotor radius; full: the full nonlinear model; ratio: double ÷ single.</p><table class=\"mt\"><thead><tr><th>wind, rotor</th><th>pivot</th><th>$R$</th><th>$G$</th><th>$\\Theta^*$ (rad)</th><th>$P^*$ (2.5), mW</th><th>full, mW</th><th>double, mW</th><th>ratio</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>6 m/s, 6.9 rpm</td><td>30 %, 18.9 m</td><td>189</td><td>190</td><td>0.713</td><td>88.93</td><td>88.62</td><td>65.17</td><td>0.735</td></tr>\n<tr><td>6 m/s, 6.9 rpm</td><td>60 %, 37.8 m</td><td>378</td><td>190</td><td>0.356</td><td>44.35</td><td>44.02</td><td>32.38</td><td>0.736</td></tr>\n<tr><td>6 m/s, 6.9 rpm</td><td>90 %, 56.7 m</td><td>567</td><td>190</td><td>0.237</td><td>29.54</td><td>29.43</td><td>21.65</td><td>0.736</td></tr>\n<tr><td>8 m/s, 9.2 rpm</td><td>30 %, 18.9 m</td><td>189</td><td>107</td><td>0.401</td><td>66.70</td><td>66.12</td><td>48.62</td><td>0.735</td></tr>\n<tr><td>8 m/s, 9.2 rpm</td><td>60 %, 37.8 m</td><td>378</td><td>107</td><td>0.200</td><td>33.26</td><td>33.17</td><td>24.39</td><td>0.735</td></tr>\n<tr><td>8 m/s, 9.2 rpm</td><td>90 %, 56.7 m</td><td>567</td><td>107</td><td>0.133</td><td>22.15</td><td>22.12</td><td>16.27</td><td>0.736</td></tr>\n<tr><td>10 m/s, 11.4 rpm</td><td>30 %, 18.9 m</td><td>189</td><td>68</td><td>0.257</td><td>53.36</td><td>53.13</td><td>39.06</td><td>0.735</td></tr>\n<tr><td>10 m/s, 11.4 rpm</td><td>60 %, 37.8 m</td><td>378</td><td>68</td><td>0.128</td><td>26.61</td><td>26.58</td><td>19.55</td><td>0.735</td></tr>\n<tr><td>10 m/s, 11.4 rpm</td><td>90 %, 56.7 m</td><td>567</td><td>68</td><td>0.085</td><td>17.72</td><td>17.71</td><td>13.03</td><td>0.736</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>",
  "chaos": "<p class=\"tcap\">Table 2. The double pendulum at resonance, $R = 1$, with gravity's push $G = 3$, each brake run from several starts: how many starts end in chaos, the mean power, and the largest Lyapunov exponent.</p><table class=\"mt\"><thead><tr><th>$\\kappa$</th><th>chaotic starts</th><th>mean power, W</th><th>largest Lyapunov exponent $\\Lambda$, s⁻¹</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>1.0</td><td>0 of 16</td><td>1.02</td><td>−2.123</td></tr>\n<tr><td>1.4</td><td>0 of 16</td><td>1.41</td><td>−0.451</td></tr>\n<tr><td>1.9</td><td>16 of 16</td><td>0.82–0.88</td><td>0.07 to 0.17</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2.8</td><td>0 of 16</td><td>0.44</td><td>−0.01 to 0.01</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>",
